* RobotWin test model library (SPICE3 / PSpice / LTspice syntax mix)
.param RTOP=10k
.model D1N4148 D(IS=2.52n RS=0.568 N=1.752 BV=100 IBV=100u CJO=4p TT=20n mfg=OnSemi)
.model Q2N3904 NPN(IS=6.734f BF=416.4 BR=.7371 VAF=74.03 CJE=4.493p CJC=3.638p XTB=1.5)
.model BS170X NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=2.1 KP=0.12 LAMBDA=0.01)
.model IRF540X VDMOS(Rg=3 Vto=4 Rd=10m Rs=8m Kp=25 lambda=.003 mfg=Vishay)
.model SW1 SW(Ron=1 Roff=1Meg Vt=2.5)

* Voltage divider with a parameter
.subckt DIVIDER IN OUT GND PARAMS: RBOT=10k
R1 IN OUT {RTOP}
R2 OUT GND {RBOT}
.ends DIVIDER

* Ideal amplifier: gain 10 with an output resistor, plus elements we cannot simulate
.subckt AMP10 INP INN OUT
E1 N1 0 INP INN 10
ROUT N1 OUT 1
CIN INP INN 1p
B1 X 0 V=V(INP)*2
K1 L1 L2 0.9
.ends AMP10

* Current mirror built from NPN transistors and a nested subcircuit
.subckt MIRROR IREF IOUT VEE
Q1 IREF IREF VEE Q2N3904
Q2 IOUT IREF VEE Q2N3904
XD IREF VEE CLAMP
.ends MIRROR

.subckt CLAMP A K
D1 A K D1N4148
.ends

* A pulse source with a continued line
.subckt CLOCK OUT GND
V1 OUT GND PULSE(0 5 0 1n 1n
+ 0.5m 1m)
.ends CLOCK

* Current-controlled sources
.subckt SENSE IN OUT MON
VS IN OUT 0
H1 MON 0 VS 100
F1 0 MON VS 0
.ends SENSE
